Add `const IS_TOUCH = ...` after constants. Use in drawHUD. Use in isTouch line as `const isTouch = IS_TOUCH;` or just remove and replace. Simpler: define `const IS_TOUCH` and later `const isTouch = IS_TOUCH;` so minimal change.

Now design HUD positions. Let's calculate touch layout more carefully with actual screenshot. Canvas is 610x343 CSS, offset 62. Scaling factor 610/1280 = .4766. HUD:
- HP at x=40, y=34 => CSS x=81, y=16. Top left, fine.
- Estus at x=50, y=VH-50=670 => CSS x=86, y=319. Joystick center: left 20 + width/2 ~62 =82, bottom 22+62=84 => center CSS (82, 259), radius 62.5. Estus at y=319 is 60 below center, near bottom edge but within joystick radius (distance 60 <62). Yes overlap. Move estus to y=125 (CSS y=60) x maybe 50. But HP bars extend to y=63 canvas => CSS 30. Estus label at fy-36=89 canvas => CSS 42, bottles at 111..125 => 53..60. So below HP, good. But world prompt etc might be around. Fine. At top-left under HP, it won't overlap joystick. Could also align with HP: fx=50, fy=125.
- Souls at bottom right x=1238, y=663..693 => CSS x=590, y=316..330. Action pad at right 14, width 280, bottom 16, height 170 => x=440..720, y=157..327. Overlap. Move souls to top-right: draw at y=105 (label 63) and number 95 => CSS label 30, number 45. But sound button DOM at top right y=16..46, x=661..720. Canvas right edge at 672, so sound overlaps game area x=661..672. Souls right-aligned at x=1238 canvas => CSS 652, under sound at y=45. Label at 30 maybe behind sound. Move souls down: label y=115, number y=145 => CSS 55,69. That's below sound (ends 46), good. But HP top-left and souls top-right fine.

- Boss bar: on touch, use narrower 420 and y = VH - 230 = 490 => CSS y=234. Its label at 480 => 229. Guard button top maybe 199..269, x 504..574. Bar x = 640-210=430..850 => CSS 267..467; no overlap with guard (504+). Great! I miscalculated before; width 420 gives right edge CSS 467, guard starts 504. Safe. And bar left edge 267, joystick right edge ~144, safe. So boss bar at y=490 canvas (CSS 234) width 420 works. It sits above action pad? Action pad y starts 157, so bar at 234 vertically overlaps but x does not. Good. It might overlap player/boss visuals but acceptable.
- Souls top right at CSS x up to 652, y 55..69. Fine.
- Estus top left CSS x 24..60, y 53..60. Fine.

- The interaction prompt "REST AT BONFIRE" is drawn at VH-236=484 canvas => CSS 231, center. That's exactly where boss bar would be on touch; but prompt shows near bonfire while boss bar not active (bonfire far away). Fine. Touch interact button at bottom center maybe obscures prompt? The DOM interact button is at bottom 30 (y~280 CSS), while prompt at 231; fine.

- Pause hint: skip on touch. Also maybe draw "II PAUSE" no need; button visible top-left.

- HP/stamina fonts on touch: increase to 13/14? Let's set text font 14, bar height 15, stamina 9, panel height maybe. But increasing might overlap. The screenshot top-left HP bar is small but readable-ish. Since we're already moving things, let's modestly enlarge: if touch, x=40, y=34, w=360, label font 14, hp bar height 14, stamina 8, sy=y+24. At CSS: width 171px, label 6.7px, still small. Font 16 => 7.6px. Not hugely better. Actual phone DPR 3, CSS 7.6px is readable. Fine. Could use 17px label and 22px? But that's a lot. We can set touch HP w=360 and label font 15.

- The HUD text "THE ASHEN ONE · LV 1" uses letterSpacing 2px; on touch set 1px.
- Souls label font 15 and number 38 on touch; CSS 7 and 18, good.
- Estus label 15.

- Boss bar label font 15.

However, using touch detection based on pointer coarse, the desktop session's resized screenshot won't show touch HUD unless we add class. That's okay. The mobile screenshot will.

Let's implement.

Pseudo:
```
